cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, cite it using the metadata below.
title: >-
  Hilbert-Polya Bridge: a self-contained numerical study of the
  graph-operator passage, the Guinand-Weil trace formula, and the
  measured boundary of lattice spectral identity
authors:
  - family-names: Isaev
    given-names: Ishak Khamzatovich
    affiliation: Independent researcher, Nalchik, Kabardino-Balkarian Republic, Russian Federation
version: 1.0.0
released: 2026-10-10
keywords:
  - Riemann Hypothesis
  - Hilbert-Polya programme
  - explicit formula
  - trace formula
  - GUE universality
  - vortex lattice
  - argument principle
license: Isaev-Proprietary-1.0
abstract: >-
  A self-contained research package walking the map from algebraic
  identities to the operator: the identity function Z_id built from the
  Gamma-ladder closures, the argument principle verified to T=1000
  (649=649), an 87-gate vortex-lattice spectral family measured in three
  independent projections, and the Guinand-Weil trace formula
  Tr e^{-xH_xi} = (1/pi) int Q(a) sin(ax) da derived from the Hadamard
  product and verified to 1.2e-5 with the Lambda(n)/sqrt(n) prime weight
  made explicit. Honest verdicts: the resonator is built and tuned
  (self-adjointness, GUE class, Dirac dynamics); the zeros are encoded,
  not generated (spectral identity and primes-in-operator measured NO
  with positive controls).
